					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12277711#post-4323915</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12277711/straight-to-vhs:sunday-dinner#post-4323915</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 06 Aug 2019 20:09:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>ValidClay</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4538622</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This might have been the best Parawatch creepypasta yet, as of August sixth at least.</p> <p>This was the first time the narrator's tone transcended a simply informative voice, or simple jadedness, and became something disgustingly real. Pervading the story, the voyeuristic fascination inherent in anyone who would watch such a movie is apparent in the narrator's tone.</p> <p>This compounds its effectiveness given the target audience, as a lot of horror readers count on creepypastas or horror work to revolve around real, horrible events such as the Byford Dolphin incident.</p> <p>The narrator seems just creepy enough to make you uncomfortable, before the twist at the end paying off this accumulated discomfort in the twist at the end, the horrifying realization you mentioned was key to creepypastas, earlier.</p> <p>I'm general, I'm so hopeful for Parawatch as a GOI, and you as a writer for it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
